      "correct": "3",
      "solution": "**Given:**\n\nExpression: 16 ÷ 2 - 7 × 15 ÷ 3 + 5 × 5 + 4 × 3 - 10\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nApply the BODMAS/BIDMAS rule (Brackets, Orders (i.e. powers and square roots, etc.), Division and Multiplication, Addition and Subtraction)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nStart with division and multiplication from left to right:\n\n16 ÷ 2 = 8\n\n7 × 15 = 105\n\n105 ÷ 3 = 35\n\n5 × 5 = 25\n\n4 × 3 = 12\n\nNow substitute these values back into the expression:\n\n8 - 35 + 25 + 12 - 10\n\nNext, perform addition and subtraction from left to right:\n\n8 - 35 = -27\n\n-27 + 25 = -2\n\n-2 + 12 = 10\n\n10 - 10 = 0\n\n**The simplified result is 0.**\n\n**The correct answer is option 3.**",
      "tags": [
        "Bodmas Rule"
      ]
